  "changes": {
    "input": "Retry EINTR; resource-pressure EAGAIN/ENOMEM back off at most25ms, returning to cancellation checks. Zero-byte read only denotes EOF. Permanent libedit input errors are recorded and thrown after callback return; active errors preserve ordinary turn-recovery semantics.",
    "presentation": "Cached prepared prefix permits append-only delivery. Known geometry keeps256 columns/final-column reservation; shifting viewports repaint. Unknown/<10 widths echo committed safe tokens and use<=80-column labelled snapshots on destructive edits/presentation changes. Raw input limit65536 and submitted bytes unchanged.",
    "destinations": "Fixed stdout/stderr identity records retain reachable boundaries; aliases share prompt and failed-record separation; new destinations receive guidance/conservative separation. No per-diagnostic stat of stdout; eligible end-of-batch redraw still inspects current geometry.",
    "warnings": "Main-thread history admission is separate from best-effort refresh; retained occurrences are retired even when refresh throws. Pending warnings retry only on real UI events or final quiescent drain.",
    "tests": "Fourteen Python3.11 enterContext calls replaced with scopes; native replacement gate proves repaint order; isolated close/reuse tests observe ownership instead of stale fd numbers."
  },
